# Language Tier Strategy

## Active Locales (Tier 1)
en, zh, ja, ko, es, de, pt, ru, tr, id

These 10 locales have demonstrated organic search traffic. All new content, features, and SEO optimizations should target these locales.

## Demoted Locales (Tier 2)  
ar, hi, th, vi

These locales show zero or near-zero organic traffic in Google Search Console. Policy:
- Do NOT create new blog posts for these locales
- Do NOT invest in translating new pSEO content for these locales
- Existing content remains indexed (no noindex)
- Sitemap priority is set to 0.1 with yearly change frequency
- Keep hreflang alternates intact

## Borderline Locales (Under Review)
fr, it

These have some impressions but very low CTR and poor positions. They remain in Tier 1 for now.

## Implementation
- Sitemap demotion: `src/app/sitemap.ts` — `DEMOTED_LOCALES` constant
- Blog creation: `blog-content.mdc` — translation targets
